# Files encrypted at rest with git-crypt.
#
# grafana-server.defaults carries NTFY_TOPIC_URL, which is a bearer
# secret rather than a mere address: ntfy topics have no access
# control, so anyone who reads the URL can both read every alert this
# fleet sends and post convincing fakes to it.
#
# It is committed rather than gitignored because deploy.sh installs
# this file verbatim to /etc/default/grafana-server. Untracked, a
# rebuild from a fresh clone would reinstate the placeholder and
# Grafana would resolve the contact point to an empty URL and drop
# every notification silently -- the exact failure this repo already
# went eighteen hours blind to once.
#
# Consequence to know about: on a clone without the key (CI, for
# instance) this file is an opaque binary blob, not text. deploy.sh
# detects that case explicitly rather than misreading ciphertext as a
# missing setting.
grafana/grafana-server.defaults filter=git-crypt diff=git-crypt
